WEBVTT

00:00.700 --> 00:07.444
This guide builds the complete SoleSense: the handle and its electronics, the pressure head, and the vibration head.

00:07.664 --> 00:11.940
Match parts by shape and number; colours are only for identification.

00:12.160 --> 00:13.646
Pause after each step.

00:16.700 --> 00:17.912
Lay out the prints.

00:18.132 --> 00:23.125
The two handle halves are zero one and zero two; the trays and shelf carry the boards.

00:23.345 --> 00:26.329
The thin rectangular spring is cassette fifty seven.

00:26.549 --> 00:28.845
Inspect its beams for cracks or bowing.

00:29.065 --> 00:31.531
Bridge fifty five is a temporary tool.

00:34.700 --> 00:37.514
Most screws come from your M two to M five kit.

00:37.734 --> 00:48.303
You still need four M three by thirty five cover screws, two M two by twenty five collar bolts and six M three heat-set inserts, plus an eighteen six fifty cell and two switches.

00:48.523 --> 00:50.617
Measure one magnet before printing.

00:54.700 --> 00:56.776
Check the modules against this list.

00:56.996 --> 00:58.492
Each has a printed seat.

00:58.712 --> 01:03.449
The magnets and micro SD board were sized from a photo, so measure them first.

01:03.669 --> 01:07.121
Leave the header pins off the ESP thirty two and the display.

01:10.700 --> 01:12.688
Wire everything on the bench first.

01:12.908 --> 01:18.613
Bridge the boost module's five volt jumper and measure its output before connecting the ESP thirty two.

01:18.833 --> 01:24.430
Follow the pin map for the display, card, button and head harness, then power up once.

01:34.700 --> 01:38.063
Heat-set six M three inserts into the lower handle bosses.

01:38.283 --> 01:41.694
Press each one straight and flush, and let the handle cool.

01:49.700 --> 01:57.749
Solder the cell tabs to the charger, strap the charger to tray zero four, and seat it in the side pod with its USB C port at the opening.

01:57.969 --> 02:00.010
Then lay the cell in its two saddles.

02:08.700 --> 02:14.995
Strap the micro SD module to tray zero five, card slot forward, and set it on its supports.

02:15.215 --> 02:22.601
Strap the boost module to shelf twenty, input end toward the heel, and screw the shelf to the four columns with M two by eight screws.

02:29.700 --> 02:36.566
Lay the ESP thirty two on tray zero three with its USB C end against the two heel stops, and strap it down.

02:36.786 --> 02:38.518
Set the tray above the battery.

02:38.738 --> 02:41.231
Its port lines up with the opening in the heel.

02:47.700 --> 02:49.302
Turn the upper handle over.

02:49.522 --> 02:56.376
Lay the display face down in its pod, pins toward the slot, and fit retainer thirty with two M two by eight screws.

02:56.596 --> 03:00.188
Drop in the button cap and glue the slide switch under the heel slot.

03:08.700 --> 03:12.811
Fit the tactile switch on button platform twenty nine and screw it down.

03:13.031 --> 03:18.553
Run the four head wires forward through wire clamp fourteen and fix it with two M two by eight screws.

03:18.773 --> 03:22.934
Leave about sixty millimetres of slack, ending in the four way connector.

03:27.700 --> 03:32.174
Lower the upper handle into place, making sure no wire is caught at the seam.

03:32.394 --> 03:37.132
Fit six M three by sixteen screws into the inserts, and tighten them evenly.

03:44.700 --> 03:50.387
Close the two collar halves around the handle shoulders and bolt them with two M two by twenty five screws.

03:50.607 --> 03:56.239
Fit the safety slider with one M two by eight screw and a washer, snug enough that it still slides.

04:03.700 --> 04:05.291
Turn the head chassis over.

04:05.511 --> 04:11.189
Fit four M three adaptor nuts, two M three sensor nuts, and two M two cassette nuts.

04:11.409 --> 04:14.770
Join adaptor forty one with four M three by eight screws.

04:23.700 --> 04:26.465
Work on carriage forty four outside the housing.

04:26.685 --> 04:28.243
Fit four M two nuts.

04:28.463 --> 04:33.064
Glue a stack of two disc magnets into the nose of holder forty six and let it cure.

04:33.284 --> 04:37.288
Then push the holder into the carriage and fit two M two by twelve screws.

04:46.700 --> 04:50.680
Place the wide moving rail against the bottoms of the two carriage posts.

04:50.900 --> 04:53.969
Drive two M two by eight screws upward from underneath.

04:54.189 --> 04:58.047
Do this outside the housing, because the floor blocks access later.

05:07.700 --> 05:10.337
Fit the small cartridge lock and leave it loose.

05:10.557 --> 05:16.047
Then lower the carriage and cassette into the chassis, holding the solid parts, never the beams.

05:16.267 --> 05:18.531
The narrow rail rests on its two pads.

05:26.700 --> 05:32.599
Fit three M three nuts in bridge fifty five and secure it with two M three by thirty five screws from below.

05:32.819 --> 05:35.080
Add the M three by twenty service pin.

05:35.300 --> 05:37.688
It should slide into the shoulder bore easily.

05:45.700 --> 05:49.512
Drive the last two M two by eight screws downward through the narrow rail.

05:49.732 --> 05:51.880
Tighten evenly with the cassette flat.

05:52.100 --> 05:55.462
Remove the service pin and check that the carriage returns freely.

06:03.700 --> 06:06.396
Solder the sensor leads and capacitor first.

06:06.616 --> 06:09.893
Seat the forty nine E with its flat face toward the magnet.

06:10.113 --> 06:17.940
Fix mount forty seven with two M three by eight screws, centred in the slots, and run the wires out the rear opening to the head connector.

06:25.700 --> 06:27.658
Remove the service pin and the bridge.

06:27.878 --> 06:35.101
Fit five M three nuts into cover forty three, lower it, and fasten all four M three by thirty five screws from underneath.

06:45.700 --> 06:48.547
Stick the motor into the pocket in dome cap eleven.

06:48.767 --> 06:52.089
Fix the driver board inside body ten with its connector.

06:52.309 --> 06:55.268
Then close the cap with three M three by eight screws.

07:07.700 --> 07:10.055
Pull the slider back and unlock the collar.

07:10.275 --> 07:13.280
Plug in the head connector and tuck the slack into the joint.

07:13.500 --> 07:18.258
Push the head on, turn the collar thirty degrees, and push the slider forward.

07:27.700 --> 07:32.891
Fit bench cartridge forty nine, turn it thirty degrees, and gently tighten the lock.

07:33.111 --> 07:34.814
Remove the whole service pin.

07:35.034 --> 07:38.942
Charge, switch on, and check that the Hall reading moves smoothly.

07:39.162 --> 07:41.541
Then calibrate against a checked balance.
